Why: Define the model tiers (strong, fast, panel) in the Subagents section; playbooks use them instead of Cursor model ids.

Problem: pstack's defaults name Cursor's model catalog (`claude-opus-*-fast`, `claude-fable-*`,
`gemini-*`), and some of its rules only make sense for those ids: family prefixes, "always use the
`-fast` id", per-vendor effort ceilings. In Claude Code, Codex, Kimi, Grok or Pi those ids don't
exist, so an agent wastes turns resolving names, or fails.

Change: model choices go through tiers defined once in poteto-mode's Subagents section:
strong (a strong model at xhigh: code, prose, judgment), fast (a fast, cheaper model at high:
mechanical edits, workers, verification, dispatch-only agents), and panel (the strongest model at
high, a fast model, and a model from another vendor). Every other default names a tier. The
settings file, role lines, budgets and `inherit-parent`/`auto` stay exactly as upstream has them.

Keep when rebasing: upstream's roles, settings-file paths and budget mechanics. Restate upstream's
new ideas in tier terms instead of dropping them (0.15.43's "Fable 5.2 is an exception" became "the
strongest model is an exception"). Drop only rules that exist because of one vendor's ids. Leave
upstream's Harness section alone; it already covers harnesses without Cursor's ids.

Reapply on a new upstream version:
1. Search the skill for `claude-`, `gemini-`, `gpt-`, `Fable`, `Opus`, `Sonnet` and `-fast`.
2. Replace each default model with its tier: code, prose and judgment -> strong; workers,
   verification and dispatch-only agents -> fast; review and design panels -> panel; the arena
   cross-judge pool -> panel without its strongest seat.
3. Replace "rejects a slug ... same family" fallbacks with "use the closest valid model from the
   error or your harness's model list, and say so". Delete family/prefix rules.
4. Rewrite vendor statements generally ("Fable counts as Claude" -> "all models from one company
   are one vendor"), or drop them when they only concern id spelling.
5. Search again: no vendor model names remain except in upstream's Harness section.
6. poteto-mode: the defaults list in the Subagents section becomes the tier definitions plus one
   line saying setup-pstack maps them; every playbook's "(default `<id>`)" becomes "(default:
   the strong tier)"; new playbooks (eval.md in 0.15.43) get the same treatment.

